From 60749aada4912827aa07ceaa21fc17401ac61725 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:13:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Stop Rep and Whop dossier saves losing or inventing data

Reputation Manager: the dossier sends a subset of identity fields, and
the save overwrote every column, so saving there emptied aliases,
trusted sources, contacts, offerings, the page phone and buyer-entered
collisions. Fields missing from the request now keep their saved value.
The dossier also keeps saved domains and competitor flags instead of
replacing them.

Whop Agent: the dossier showed a hardcoded 20% / 3 month offer, never
loaded the real one, and the server dropped the offer and bridge URL it
sent. It also always failed to save once connected, because it posted
to the connect route without a key. It now starts empty, loads and saves
through the save-offer and bridge routes (keeping tenure, cooldown and
field mapping), only reconnects when a key is typed, and requires all
three offer fields or none.

Remove the whopSaveOffer and whopBridgeDestinationUrl writebacks: the
first filled gaps with a guessed 20% discount, the second could route
member events to an unvalidated URL. Neither fact was written anywhere.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BpwEEhpC2kCNG3EYk41xNL
