From 562047cc3ab5aea2bcdcc62f90e7d8aa512d7b51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:44:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Show guesses as suggestions, let users pick, and stop
 inventing answers

The dossiers pre-filled every fact whatever its score, so a 30% guess
looked the same as a real answer, and findings below the auto-apply
threshold never reached the user at all. Now one trust rule
(isFactTrusted) decides both auto-apply and pre-fill; everything else
comes back as a suggestion shown beside its field with its source and
score, and users can use it or say it's not right.

- POST /api/engagements/[id]/facts/[key] records confirm/edit/reject.
  Dossier saves record what the user did with each suggestion.
  upsertClientFact no longer lets a crawl or harvest overwrite an
  edited fact or re-suggest the value a user rejected.
- Pin-Down, ICP Lock and Rep Onboarding show suggestions; offer, product
  and operator fields are editable in the dossiers (they were display
  only, so a missed price couldn't be entered there).
- Offer vertical uses a fixed list (src/lib/verticals.ts, a draft to
  review); Jev classifies site copy into it and Leak Map groups
  benchmarks by it, so spellings of the same vertical share a group.
- Cold Open: Jev suggests which live campaign each ICP maps to, a team
  size band per ICP, and scores Claude's proposed exclusions.
- Showtime: SMS, ad-data, brief destination and video platform are
  suggested from what's connected, only where that tool can deliver.
  Leak Map suggests the signed-in user's email for reports.

Stop inventing answers: Pin-Down no longer defaults offer name to the
client name, traffic temperature to warm (also in the writeback and
details route), or SMS/ad-data to none and briefs to slack. Rep no
longer fills the sole authority with the client name or 'Workspace
Owner'. ICP Lock no longer invents a Professional tone.

The ICP Lock dossier's voice edits were dropped and its daily-send
section didn't match the stored shape; both now save through the Voice
Capture and Daily Send services, keeping saved templates and the
live-send switch. Copy mode defaults to generate unless every ICP has
templates, since upload with none skips every lead.

Briefs sent to 'email' (offered by Pin-Down) or calendar_event with no
Slack fallback were silently dropped; the dossier now offers only Slack
or a CRM note, the route rejects others, and deliverBrief throws.

