From 2a3e00402b33b144a3239caec04e37b832376d8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:53:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Show each worker's real status and close setup gaps on
 skill pages

The dossiers' '7/7 Active', '6/6' and '15/15 Active' were typed-in
text. Skills are on by default, so the count said nothing about the
ones blocked by missing fields. GET /api/engagements/[id]/worker-status
reports each worker as ready, needs setup (with what's missing) or off,
and a shared WorkerStatusGrid shows it in all four dossiers, refreshed
after each save. Save messages no longer say 'armed'.

Pin-Down's save re-enabled all five Showtime workers and Whop's connect
all fifteen, which silently undid any worker a user had switched off;
each now enables only its own worker. Pin-Down again refuses to save
without a website (dropped in the dossier rewrite).

- Pre-Call Read's page can now set where briefs land and the Slack
  webhook (its two required fields), with the CRM-note suggestion.
- Pile-On's page takes the chosen platform's key and the Twilio/GHL
  sending details. Choosing a platform whose key was saved earlier now
  marks it connected (it stayed blocked on 'no credential' before), and
  saving the Twilio SIDs re-runs the A2P status check.
- Voice Capture shows the voice read from the website and records the
  decision.
- Source Connect starts with one row per locked ICP, on Apify when its
  key is connected.

