From 04dbe75db75c44869d09ab63cbeeb1d8d140c1cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:59:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Connect accounts inside the dossiers; surface Twilio
 rejections and all Whop plans

Pin-Down's and Cold Open's '+ Connect' sent users to Settings -> Apps,
which saves a key to the shared store without attaching it to the
client or harvesting it. Both dossiers now connect in place with
CredentialRow (paste, reuse saved, or OAuth sign-in returning to the
dossier), for booking, email/CRM and hosting in Pin-Down and the
sending tool in ICP Lock, whose save now stores the chosen platform.

A key saved before its platform was picked stayed 'not connected'
because the marker is only set at key-save time.
syncMarkersForChosenPlatforms runs after Pin-Down, Pile-On and Edit
Stack Settings save platform choices.

Twilio: a FAILED A2P campaign maps to 'brand_registered', which read
as progress. The raw status is now kept and Pile-On shows a rejected
or in-review campaign. Saving the SIDs from Edit Stack Settings re-runs
the check too.

Whop: read one page of up to 50 plans instead of one (page size and
pagination still unverified against Whop's docs). One plan fills the
offer price; several are offered in Pin-Down as a pick instead of
guessing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BpwEEhpC2kCNG3EYk41xNL
