From 18b85f0bf6c0cda93c61ba2994ad19cfdc3ccd41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 02:22:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Slack: sign in with Slack and pick a channel, or keep a
 webhook

Pre-Call Read's "Where briefs land" step now offers two ways to reach a
client's Slack: sign in (Composio "slack" connection) and pick a public
channel harvested from the workspace, or paste an incoming-webhook URL.
Saving one clears the other.

- slack-delivery.ts: postToClientSlack posts through the connection
  (chat.postMessage, text only; buttons need the app's own interactivity
  URL) when a channel is picked, the webhook otherwise; throws on failure.
- Briefs, resend, notifications and the pending-action digest use it.
- The Slack harvest paginates channels and stores them as slackChannels.
- The route only accepts a channel from that list.
- Completeness and status checks accept a webhook or a connected channel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BpwEEhpC2kCNG3EYk41xNL
